# .agent-rules - agent-mem shared team memory
# Track this file in git to share rules across your team without SQLite binary conflicts.

architecture/anchor-garbage-collection = Auto-Poda de Reglas Zombis (clean and post-commit hook): inspects anchor paths against filesystem and git deleted files, auto-archiving stale memories with [file_deleted: <paths>] without leaving working trees dirty or breaking multi-branch isolation
architecture/canonical-project-registry = Canonical project registry in ~/.config/agent-mem/projects.json resolves symlinks/case-folding and anchors by git remote URL, eliminating duplication while keeping zero overhead on reads. (@ src/registry.rs:1)
architecture/clustered-knowledge-hypergraph = Clustered Knowledge Hypergraph (PRAGMA user_version=3) supporting 4 entity kinds (rule, decision, gotcha, pattern), typed relations (relates_to, mitigates, depends_on, supersedes), code anchor filtering with 1-hop expansion cutting token overhead by >95%, and plain-text Team Git Sync. (@ src/store.rs:162)
architecture/mcp-de-provisioning = agent-mem mcp uninstall [client|all] provides zero-residue de-provisioning across 17 AI editors preserving unrelated servers, with binary removal via cargo uninstall agent-mem
[decision] architecture/mcp-dual-era = Stateless dual-era MCP supports legacy 2024-11-05 initialization and modern 2026-07-28 per-request metadata with server/discover, cold-path validation, cacheable discovery, and no new runtime dependencies. (@ src/mcp.rs:9)
[decision] architecture/mcp-manage-lifecycle = mem_manage tool provides full lifecycle control (archive, unarchive, delete, relate, unrelate) in a single consolidated schema (<1450 chars ratchet) with atomic SQLite transactions and .agent-rules sync. (@ src/mcp.rs:135)
architecture/mcp-strict-storage-integrity = agent-mem MCP propagates all SQLite I/O failures (isError: true) instead of swallowing them, enforces write consistency across relations and .agent-rules export, and validates scopes strictly
[decision] architecture/zero-friction-init = Single-command init with auto-configured AI editor MCP clients and robust git worktree/submodule commondir hook resolution (@ src/init.rs:60)
[decision] benchmark/competitive-suite = Automated benchmark suite (cargo bench) measuring sub-microsecond B-tree reads (1.38µs), BM25 (294µs), hypergraph traversals (1.00µs), and 99% anchor token reduction (@ benches/bench_suite.rs:1)
[decision] decision/hook = add zero-overhead git lifecycle auto-capture post-commit hook (@ src/cli.rs:1, src/hook.rs:1, src/init.rs:1)
feature/selective-context = Selective context filtering via git diff or files: matches anchored rules, expands 1-hop hypergraph relations, includes universal rules, 90%+ token reduction
release/v1.1.0 = Release v1.1.0 published: benchmark suite (cargo bench), AI client auto-setup, thread-safe test isolation, and GitHub release artifacts

# Relations
[rel] architecture/zero-friction-init -> relates_to -> architecture/canonical-project-registry
[rel] benchmark/competitive-suite -> relates_to -> architecture/zero-friction-init

